		{
			"id": "112158671586861607",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@groxx/112158671539145980",
			"author": {
				"name": "groxx",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@groxx",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-25T22:25:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> worst-case fast also gets you an *unbelievably amazing* experience on the best-case stuff.</p><p>I love using low end hardware to build things. You find out what hurts your end result FAR earlier, when you're more easily able to fix it.  And then the final result absolutely screams on decent machines, and that's an amazing feeling.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112158711347490495",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@boulder/112158711123236979",
			"author": {
				"name": "4everpushingaboulder",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@boulder",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-25T22:35:14.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> app dev has blamed performance on network, database, IO, cpu for years, while writing heavy code optimized for their test lab instead of production. </p><p> Cloud based, microcoded, API,  shared service enterprise buss were supposed to be the fix to keep us dumb infrastructure folks from being in the way. </p><p>Always told people it’s just 4th grade math. 8 bits per byte. Do the math.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112158721807743952",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@danherbert/112158721779711371",
