		{
			"id": "112158749896006773",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@JeffGrigg/112158749849404377",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jeff Grigg",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@JeffGrigg",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/426/648/562/796/087/original/82d4ec377078c166.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-25T22:45:05.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>As I was explaining to our local water and sewer utility, …</p><p>I'm paying my monthly bill from a small city in Argentina. I don't want or need a full-screen video of local water features to play before you allow me to access and pay my (typically less than $100) monthly bill! And some of your local customers, like my parents, are *still on dial-up*. With *OLD* computers. Like \"should be recycled\" computers that Barely Work!!!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112158760493648474",
			"parentId": "112158749896006773",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@JeffGrigg/112158760465111247",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jeff Grigg",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@JeffGrigg",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/426/648/562/796/087/original/82d4ec377078c166.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-25T22:47:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>Now as to why I would be paying local mid-Texas utilities from South America, or Ireland, or across the date line in New Zealand, …</p><p>Well, I have my reasons.<br>(And they're none of the water company's business.)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112158933752339929",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite/112158933712442104",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jared White (ResistanceNet ✊)",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/552/988/169/598/original/863bd81d9ad9d7b6.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2024-03-25T23:31:50.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Funny about that year mentioned in <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>slightlyoff</span></a></span>'s article, 2015.</p><p>I was told in 2015 by a “CTO” that I should ditch my Ruby on Rails skills, learn how to write JSON APIs in Node, and build all my UIs in AngularJS going forward. This was the future!</p><p>He may have been broadly right about the popularity of Node, but the rest of that mindset turned out to be a minefield of antipatterns. While today I'm no particular fan of Rails, it's wild how SSR (plus SSG) is all the rage once again.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
