			"date": "2024-03-26T08:47:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> we lack the vocabulary (and metrics) to make meaningful statements about our software's efficiency.</p><p>By rights, Elixir should be running away with things based on Phoenix's performance alone, but we're not hiring for efficiency. We're hiring for popularity and/or groupthink.</p>",
