			"date": "2024-03-26T10:40:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Twitter and WhatsApp both grew quickly early on because they worked on lowend phones. Twitter’s original text-only 140 character limit was strategically intentionally aligned with what SMS could do.</p><p>WhatsApp ran as a Java app on non-Android, non-iOS phones.</p>",
